# SY-1 — SysML block definition diagram: the system and its blocks.

direction: down

title: |md
  # SY-1 — SysML block definition: the system and its blocks
  A filled diamond is composition: the whole owns the part. A dashed arrow is a compile-time dependency.
| {near: top-center}

classes: {
  block: {style: {fill: "#FFFFFF"; stroke: "#3F6FB5"}}
  external: {style: {fill: "#F2F4F7"; stroke: "#77808D"}}
  owns: {source-arrowhead: {shape: diamond; style.filled: true}; target-arrowhead: {shape: arrow}}
  uses: {style: {stroke-dash: 4; stroke: "#3F6FB5"}}
}

system: |md
  «block» **Pacenotes System**

  pacenote packages for rally games, from one server to many game folders
| {class: block}

installer: |md
  «block» **Installer** — Windows GUI

  *parts:* wizard (nine pages, three routes), worker thread, WinHTTP client, cache, ledger, engine, restore, run log

  *constraints:* .exe under 700 kB; no tokio, reqwest, rustls, hyper or GUI crate; imports only DLLs Windows ships
| {class: block}

protocol: |md
  «block» **Shared Protocol** — the shared/ crate

  *values:* Manifest, PackageInfo, GameSchema, KeyStatus, ConflictReport, ApiError

  *constraint:* serde only; no I/O, no async, no HTTP
| {class: block}

server: |md
  «block» **Package Server** — one static binary

  *parts:* routes, auth (decide), store (manifest gen), reports (validate, rate limit), admin CLI

  *constraint:* TLS is the reverse proxy's job, not its own
| {class: block}

game: |md
  «block» **Game Installation** — external

  the game folder a run targets; `.pacenotes/` holds every trace of the installer
| {class: external}

catalogue: |md
  «block» **Package Catalogue** — the data root

  zips, sidecars, schemas, the generated `manifest.json`, `motd/<lang>.txt`, `reports/*.jsonl`
| {class: block}

authdb: |md
  «block» **Auth Database** — libSQL

  tokens and grants; raw keys are never stored
| {class: block}

system -> installer: "" {class: owns}
system -> protocol: "" {class: owns}
system -> server: "" {class: owns}
system -> catalogue: "" {class: owns}
system -> authdb: "" {class: owns}
installer -> protocol: "«use»" {class: uses}
server -> protocol: "«use»" {class: uses}
installer -> game: "writes only here"
server -> catalogue: "reads; manifest gen writes manifest.json"
server -> authdb: "SQL"
